[
  ["", {"__cerberus_parentSpanID": "", "__cerberus_spanID": "bbbb", "__cerberus_traceID": "a0000000000000000000000000000001"}, "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z", 0],
  ["", {"__cerberus_parentSpanID": "", "__cerberus_spanID": "cccc", "__cerberus_traceID": "a0000000000000000000000000000001"}, "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z", 0]
]
-- chplan --
Filter predicate=FnNot(FnMapContainsKey(SpanAttributes, "http.method"))
  Scan(otel_traces)
-- parity_exempt --
reason: reference-fetch-layer
detail: `{ span.http.method = nil }` is upstream's unary OpNotExists, which tests for the Static string "nil" that only the fetch layer's key-absence iterator writes, so the in-process engine matches nothing at all
